  <entry>
    <id>http://arxiv.org/abs/2602.23058v2</id>
    <title>GeoWorld: Geometric World Models</title>
    <updated>2026-05-17T06:55:06Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2602.23058v2" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/2602.23058v2" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>Energy-based predictive world models provide a powerful approach for multi-step visual planning by reasoning over latent energy landscapes rather than generating pixels. However, existing approaches face two major challenges: (i) their latent representations are typically learned in Euclidean space, neglecting the underlying geometric and hierarchical structure among states, and (ii) they struggle with long-horizon prediction, which leads to rapid degradation across extended rollouts. To address these challenges, we introduce GeoWorld, a geometric world model that preserves geometric structure and hierarchical relations through a Hyperbolic JEPA, which maps latent representations from Euclidean space onto hyperbolic manifolds. We further introduce Geometric Reinforcement Learning for energy-based optimization, enabling stable multi-step planning in hyperbolic latent space. Extensive experiments on CrossTask and COIN demonstrate around 3% SR improvement in 3-step planning and 2% SR improvement in 4-step planning compared to the state-of-the-art V-JEPA 2. Project website: https://steve-zeyu-zhang.github.io/GeoWorld.</summary>
    <category term="cs.CV" scheme="http://arxiv.org/schemas/atom"/>
    <category term="cs.RO" scheme="http://arxiv.org/schemas/atom"/>
    <published>2026-02-26T14:42:53Z</published>
    <arxiv:comment>Accepted to CVPR 2026</arxiv:comment>
    <arxiv:primary_category term="cs.CV"/>
    <author>
      <name>Zeyu Zhang</name>
    </author>
    <author>
      <name>Danning Li</name>
    </author>
    <author>
      <name>Ian Reid</name>
    </author>
    <author>
      <name>Richard Hartley</name>
